__pycache__
venv
.venv
.idea
.ipynb_checkpoints
spotify_details.json
.cache
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
*.pkl
# Decode caches (<audio>.<rate>.npy), ~7.7x the mp3 -- including the ones the
# benchmark leaves beside the committed mp3s in training/eval_audio/.
*.npy
# D12's extractor cell cache (<audio>.<decoder>.mertcells.npz), the same rule one
# layer up: derived from the audio, machine-local, never committed.
*.mertcells.npz
report.json
# The Raveform corpus: ~90 GB, machine-local, never committed.  The ten eval-set
# tracks are the deliberate exception and live in training/eval_audio/.
#
# Labels are committed, songs are not -- so hand-authored annotations are tracked
# where the rest of the dataset's labels live.  Re-including a path this deep
# needs a rung per level: a directory ignored with a trailing slash is pruned
# before git ever looks inside it, so each level ignores its *contents* and
# re-admits the one child below.  Nothing but *.hand.json is ever re-admitted;
# the published segments.json stays ignored (widening this to it is one line).
#
# The first rung re-admits the directory rather than its contents, because
# `training/data/` is also excluded from .git/info/exclude on at least one
# machine; a rule there would prune the walk before any rung below could be
# reached, and .gitignore is the only one of the two that every clone gets.
!training/data/
training/data/*
!training/data/raveform/
training/data/raveform/*
!training/data/raveform/annotations/
training/data/raveform/annotations/*
!training/data/raveform/annotations/*.hand.json
